<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!-- Retention and Churn console: the share of each acquisition cohort still
     active, by month since first purchase. Two series, one per cohort year.

     THIS TILE IS LIFETIME SCOPED, BY DESIGN, AND THAT IS ENFORCED BY ITS QUERY,
     NOT BY ITS PARAMETER LIST. A retention curve is a lifetime measurement of a
     fixed cohort: filtering it by risk band or loyalty tier would reshape the
     very population whose survival is being tracked, and the score date is a
     scoring cutoff rather than a cohort boundary, so none of the four console
     controls has a defined meaning here.

     So the four console parameters ARE declared below, exactly as on the other
     five tiles, and are then referenced NOWHERE: not in the query, not in an
     expression, not in a printWhenExpression. The tile's output is therefore
     identical whatever the strip has selected. This is the same shape Phase 1
     used for trs_liability and trs_lease_expiry, both of which declare the full
     console parameter set and then ignore the parts their SQL has no column for.

     The declarations are NOT optional decoration. gen_dashboard.py hands every
     report dashlet the whole "filters" array as its input parameters and wires
     every control to every report dashlet's @applyParams, with no check that the
     tile declares the name. A tile with no parameter block would still be handed
     all four values; declaring them gives that blind wiring somewhere to land.

     No input controls are attached to this tile (no Attach-ChurnControls call),
     which is correct and sufficient: a declared parameter that nothing reads
     needs no control to populate it, and an unattached parameter is never
     prompted. Verified after the change by GET on the report unit
     (hasInputControls = False) and by recomposing and re-rendering the tile.

     NO ZERO GUARD ON THE SERIES VALUE, AND THAT IS DELIBERATE. The console rule
     is that a null on the first row fails to register a series and shifts the
     seriesColor bindings, so chart values are normally coalesced to zero. Here
     active_pct cannot be null: the upstream build already wraps the divide in
     NULLIF, and a row only exists in the cohort aggregate when the cell has at
     least one customer in it, so the denominator is never zero and never absent.
     A guard here would be dead code that a later reader would have to reason
     about, so the reasoning is written down instead. The series and category
     keys are still derived with String.valueOf, which is null safe in its own
     right, and the query's ORDER BY cohort_year fixes the registration order so
     2019 binds to seriesColor order 0 and 2020 to order 1.

     The 2020 cohort is a partial year and only has months 0 to 11 in the source,
     so its line legitimately stops short of the 2019 line rather than dropping
     to zero.

     JR7 native line plot: showLines/showShapes are the valid flags on a line
     plot (showTickMarks/showTickLabels are REJECTED there per
     jr7-valid-elements.md 3d). Chart is in the title band, so
     evaluationTime="Report". -->
<jasperReport name="chn_cohorts" language="java" pageWidth="1000" pageHeight="380" columnWidth="980" leftMargin="10" rightMargin="10" topMargin="10" bottomMargin="10">
	<parameter name="chn_score_date" class="java.util.Collection"/>
	<parameter name="p_regions" class="java.util.Collection"/>
	<parameter name="chn_tier" class="java.util.Collection"/>
	<parameter name="chn_band" class="java.util.Collection"/>

	<query language="SQL"><![CDATA[
SELECT cohort_year, months_since_first, active_pct
FROM dash_cohort
WHERE months_since_first BETWEEN 0 AND 18
ORDER BY cohort_year, months_since_first
	]]></query>

	<field name="cohort_year" class="java.lang.Integer"/>
	<field name="months_since_first" class="java.lang.Integer"/>
	<field name="active_pct" class="java.math.BigDecimal"/>

	<title height="360">
		<element kind="image" x="0" y="0" width="44" height="44" scaleImage="RetainShape" hImageAlign="Left" vImageAlign="Top"><expression><![CDATA["repo:/images/actian_logo"]]></expression></element>
		<element kind="staticText" x="0" y="2" width="980" height="22" fontSize="16.0" bold="true" forecolor="#1F4E79" hTextAlign="Center"><text><![CDATA[Active Share by Months Since First Purchase]]></text></element>
		<element kind="staticText" x="0" y="26" width="980" height="14" fontSize="9.0" forecolor="#5B7DA6" hTextAlign="Center" vTextAlign="Middle"><text><![CDATA[2019 vs 2020 acquisition cohorts. Months since first purchase along the bottom, active share up the side.]]></text></element>

		<element kind="chart" chartType="line" x="0" y="48" width="980" height="312" evaluationTime="Report">
			<dataset kind="category">
				<series>
					<seriesExpression><![CDATA[String.valueOf($F{cohort_year})]]></seriesExpression>
					<categoryExpression><![CDATA[String.valueOf($F{months_since_first})]]></categoryExpression>
					<valueExpression><![CDATA[$F{active_pct}]]></valueExpression>
				</series>
			</dataset>
			<plot showLines="true" showShapes="true" valueAxisTickLabelMask="#,##0'%'">
				<seriesColor order="0" color="#0550DC"/>
				<seriesColor order="1" color="#1DB6C0"/>
			</plot>
		</element>
	</title>

</jasperReport>
